<section class="bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 py-16">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-6 text-center">How to Save TikTok Videos Without Watermark</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 text-center mb-10">Last updated: <%= currentYear %></p>

    <div class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
        TikTok is full of entertaining and educational short videos. Sometimes you want to save a clip to watch offline or back up your own uploads. This guide shows how to download TikTok videos in MP4 and remove the watermark for clips you own or have rights to use.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-8 mb-4">Understanding TikTok watermarks</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">TikTok adds a watermark with the creator's username and the TikTok logo. This helps credit creators. You should only remove watermarks from videos you created or have permission to edit. Removing watermarks from other creators' content without permission can violate TikTok's terms and copyright.</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-8 mb-4">Downloading your own TikTok videos</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">If you uploaded the video, you can download it from TikTok's app without a watermark. Go to your profile, open the video, tap the three dots, and select <strong>Save video</strong>. If the save-with-watermark option is on, turn it off in settings.</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-8 mb-4">Using ClipVault for public TikTok links</h2>
      <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 space-y-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
        <li>Open TikTok and tap <strong>Share</strong>, then <strong>Copy link</strong>.</li>
        <li>Visit <a href="/" class="text-sky-600 dark:text-sky-400 hover:underline"><%= siteTitle %></a>.</li>
        <li>Paste the link and click <strong>Get Video</strong>.</li>
        <li>Select an MP4 option. Some sources provide watermark-free versions when available.</li>
        <li>Download the file to your device.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-8 mb-4">Best practices</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
        <li>Always credit the original creator if you share the clip.</li>
        <li>Do not upload unwatermarked versions of other people's work as your own.</li>
        <li>Use downloaded clips for personal offline viewing unless you have a license.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-8 mb-4">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <details class="bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 p-4">
          <summary class="font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white cursor-pointer">Is it legal to remove the TikTok watermark?</summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 text-sm">For your own videos, yes. For others' videos, only with permission. Unauthorized removal can be copyright infringement.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 p-4">
          <summary class="font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white cursor-pointer">Why is my TikTok link not working?</summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 text-sm">Make sure the video is public. Private, deleted, or age-restricted videos may not be accessible.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 p-4">
          <summary class="font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white cursor-pointer">Can I download TikTok videos on iPhone?</summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 text-sm">Yes, use Safari or Chrome on your iPhone. The download saves to your Files or Photos app.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
